---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-markdown-editor</code> is a form field for rich text, such as a
  ticket description or release notes. People edit formatted text directly,
  the way they would in a word processor; the value is Markdown, so it stores
  as plain text and reads back the same in <code>wc-markdown</code>.
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Toolbar</strong>: text style, bold, italic, strikethrough, inline
    code, link, lists, checklist, quote, code block, table, divider and
    mention. While the caret is in a table, a <em>Table</em> menu adds and
    removes rows and columns.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Selection bubble</strong>: select text to format it in place.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Slash menu</strong>: type <code>/</code> to insert a block.
    Markdown shortcuts such as <code>## </code>, <code>- </code>,
    <code>1. </code>, <code>&gt; </code> and <code>**bold**</code> work as you
    type.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Block handle</strong>: hover a block to drag it, or press
    <strong>+</strong> to insert a block below.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Link</strong>: the toolbar button, the bubble or
    <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>/<kbd>⌘</kbd>+<kbd>K</kbd> open the link editor. Only web,
    email and relative addresses are accepted.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>View source</strong>: the last toolbar button shows the Markdown,
    which you can edit directly.
  </li>
</ul>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-markdown-editor
    id="md-editor"
    label="Description"
    helper-text="Type / for blocks, select text to format, @ to mention."
    style="display:block; width: 100%;"
  ></wc-markdown-editor>
  <script is:inline>
    document.getElementById('md-editor').value = [
      '## Steps to reproduce',
      '',
      '1. Open the **billing** page as an admin',
      '2. Export last month as *CSV*',
      '',
      '- [x] Reproduced on staging',
      '- [ ] Reproduced on production',
      '',
      '| Region | Status |',
      '| --- | --- |',
      '| EU | Failing |',
      '| US | OK |',
    ].join('\n');
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3 class="text-title-medium">Without the toolbar</h3>

<p>
  <code>hide-toolbar</code> leaves a clean writing surface. Formatting stays
  available from the selection bubble, the slash menu, Markdown shortcuts and
  keyboard shortcuts.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-markdown-editor
    label="Notes"
    hide-toolbar
    rows="3"
    placeholder="Write a note. Select text to format it."
    style="display:block; width: 100%;"
  ></wc-markdown-editor>
</DemoComponentCard>
